{%- comment -%}
  Business identity in the footer, on every page.

  WHY IT EXISTS. Google Merchant Center suspended the account for
  Misrepresentation on 6 Aug 2026. The policy requires a merchant to "describe
  your business on your website" with "updated contact information and a clear
  explanation of what your company does". The About page did the second half
  well and the first half was missing entirely: the address, the phone number
  and hello@theyoink.com appeared ZERO times on the homepage, the About page and
  the contact page. The contact page was a bare form — name, email, comment,
  submit — with no way to tell who you were writing to.

  A shopper could not reach this business except by filling in a form and hoping.
  That is what an automated check sees as a store with no verifiable identity.

  IN THE LAYOUT, NOT THE FOOTER SECTION GROUP. `sections/footer-group.json` is
  owned by the theme editor and repo edits to it are silently ignored — a block
  added there works until someone opens the editor. Rendered from theme.liquid
  it is repo-controlled and cannot be lost, which is the same reason
  `aj-email-popup` lives there. See the comment above it.

  VALUES COME FROM THE SHOP RECORD, never hardcoded, so the footer cannot drift
  from what Shopify tells payment processors and Google.

  NO STREET ADDRESS. `shop.address` holds a residential address; city, province
  and country give Google a verifiable location without putting a home on the
  public web. A postal address still has to appear in MARKETING EMAIL under
  CAN-SPAM — that is a separate gap, and it needs a business or mailbox address
  rather than this one.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="aj-contact">
  <div class="page-width">
    <p class="aj-contact__label">Contact us</p>
    <ul class="aj-contact__list">
      {%- if shop.email != blank -%}
        <li>
          <a href="mailto:{{ shop.email }}">{{ shop.email }}</a>
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.phone != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          THE SHOP RECORD STORES IT UNPUNCTUATED — "4794020530" — and printing
          that raw undercuts the one thing this block exists to do. A phone
          number nobody has bothered to format reads as machine output, not as a
          business you can ring.

          `tel:` takes the bare digits; only the label is punctuated. Anything
          that is not a ten-digit US number is printed exactly as stored rather
          than forced into a shape it does not have.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign tel = shop.phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' | remove: '.' | remove: '+'
          assign tel_len = tel | size
          assign phone_label = shop.phone
          if tel_len == 10
            assign p1 = tel | slice: 0, 3
            assign p2 = tel | slice: 3, 3
            assign p3 = tel | slice: 6, 4
            assign phone_label = '(' | append: p1 | append: ') ' | append: p2 | append: '-' | append: p3
          endif
        -%}
        <li>
          <a href="tel:{{ tel }}">{{ phone_label }}</a>
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if shop.address.city != blank -%}
        <li class="aj-contact__where">
          {{- shop.address.city }}, {{ shop.address.province }}, {{ shop.address.country -}}
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/contact">Contact form</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    A band above the footer's own content, not inside it — the footer section is
    editor-owned and its internals can be rearranged at any time, so this cannot
    depend on where its columns sit.
  */
  .aj-contact {
    border-block-start: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.12);
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  .aj-contact__label {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    padding-block-end: 0.3rem;
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Same purple label with a yellow rule as the mega menu and the category
     drill-down. One section-label vocabulary across the site. */
  .aj-contact__label::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  .aj-contact__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .aj-contact__list a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-block-end: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.25);
  }

  .aj-contact__list a:hover {
    border-block-end-color: currentcolor;
  }

  .aj-contact__where {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* On a phone the row becomes a short stack rather than a wrapped line, so the
     email and the phone number each get their own tap target. */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .aj-contact__list {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
